    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0283" n="275" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg275"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/9567: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander in Chief of the United States Asiatic
                        Fleet</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Yarnell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval
                        Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="68" xml:id="d277-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-22T12:15:00+08:00">August 22, 1937—12:15
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 22—6 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>0022. Joint letter signed by American, British and French Admirals<anchor n="69"
                        xml:id="d277-f2"/> has been sent to Admiral Hasegawa protesting against
                    presence of a Japanese destroyer about 300 yards down stream from <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Augusta</hi> and requesting that all Japanese vessels be
                    kept below Hongkew Creek. Substance of reply will be communicated when
                    received.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
